//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_METHOD_DEF_RUNTIME", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-19 for the Pine parity programme (libraries chain, admit:method-def), capture queue
// rows Q-MD-2a / Q-MD-2b. NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW. No licence-held text.
//
// --- A SECOND SCRIPT FOR THE `method-def` ROW, DRAWN BY THE RUNTIME LANE ---
// Measured 2026-11-19 at engine 80: the six committed captures whose scripts declare a `method` and grade MATCH
// (zero-lag-ma-trend-levels, ict-killzones-pivots-tfo, pro-trading-art, RDDT and SPY each) are all drawn by the
// HOST lane, so none is evidence for a runtime capability; the one method-def script the runtime lane draws
// (volatility-trend-score-backquant) is INCONCLUSIVE on an untitled plot the harness cannot pair. This probe
// declares two methods on a user type whose state carries across bars (`var`), which only the runtime lane
// draws. Rows:
//   A00  bar_index                                 control
//   M01  a.total after `a.add(close)` each bar     the running total of close
//   M02  a.mean()                                  the running mean of close
//   M03  a.n                                       the count, bar_index + 1
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D and AMEX:SPY 1D, each from the listing, inputs at defaults (none), after the close. Read
// every plot on every bar as full float64 text. If a row does not compile, record the error text and the line,
// remove only that row, and capture the rest.
type Acc
    float total = 0.0
    int n = 0

method add(Acc this, float x) =>
    this.total += x
    this.n += 1
    this

method mean(Acc this) =>
    this.n > 0 ? this.total / this.n : na

var Acc a = Acc.new()
a.add(close)
plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")
plot(a.total, "M01_running_total_of_close")
plot(a.mean(), "M02_running_mean_of_close")
plot(a.n, "M03_count")
